[TITLE]
Island of junctions J3-J4 cut off from the reservoir by CLOSED pipes.
Without disconnection handling this network makes the hydraulic matrix
ill-conditioned (Error 110): the island's 16 parallel internal pipes are capped
by pipecoeff() at a head loss gradient of RQTOL/Hexp = 2^-24 exactly (RQTOL
below is 1.852*2^-24), giving the island block a conductance of exactly
16*2^24 = 2^28, while the closed boundary pipes couple the island to the
network at only 1/CBIG = 1e-8, which vanishes below half an ulp when added to
2^28 - all Cholesky quantities are exact powers of two (sqrt(2^28) = 2^14), so
the island's final pivot is exactly 0.0 on any IEEE-754 platform and in any
elimination order. With disconnection handling the island's heads are fixed at
its highest junction elevation instead and the run ends with warning 3.

